  <main class="container" id="main">
    <section class="gallery-intro"><p class="eyebrow">A flexible CMDB. Three perspectives.</p><h1>Your CMDB. Your data.<br><em>Your model.</em></h1><p>Three directions for the same story: authoritative and reference data, schema-bound or schema-free, connected through relations. Open a study to see how the CMDB, its content, and its connections come together.</p></section>
    <div class="concept-grid">$cards</div>
    <section class="review-notes"><div><span class="eyebrow">What to look for</span><h2>The data.<br>The structure.<br>The connections.</h2></div><div><p>Each complete scrolling study gives data ownership, schema choices, and relationships their own space. The same CMDB can hold data whose authority lives here or elsewhere, with structured and free-form content side by side.</p><p><strong>Confluence</strong> is the calmest direction. <strong>Orbit</strong> makes the strongest statement about the hub. <strong>Fabric</strong> gives the model an architectural, editorial character. Defined and open record motifs carry the new focus into every illustration.</p><p>The illustrations describe the product’s ideas. The source and schema labels in the example model explain a possible setup, rather than showing an existing graph interface or automatic source management.</p></div></section>
  </main>
  <footer class="container gallery-footer"><span>Hubuum / Landing page exploration</span><span>Shared story. Original vector artwork. Three distinct directions.</span></footer>
